fast as an ordinary miner. While they prefer mining, they still make good, fast glass makers.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits5=Friendly\r\ncontainer.sim.traits6=Friendly folk are always out to make friends. They will rarely have poor relationships with other folk and become unhappy when they have no friends.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits7=Green Thumb\r\ncontainer.sim.traits8=Folk with a green thumb make much better crop farmers. They can plant, plough and harvest twice as fast, meaning you make twice the amount of produce.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits9=Hates the Outdoors\r\ncontainer.sim.traits10=Folk that hate the outdoors tend to warp more frequently They dislike open spaces, and hate working on farms.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits11=Loves the Outdoors\r\ncontainer.sim.traits12=Folk that love the outdoors love taking leisurely strolls. They love open spaces, and working outside will make their day.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits13=Night Owl\r\ncontainer.sim.traits14=Night Owl folk won't spend much time indoors upon nightfall. They will wander during the night. Night Owl folk will continue terraforming and building work throughout the night.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits15=Religious\r\ncontainer.sim.traits16=Religious folk like to visit church daily to pray. Being unable to do so makes them unhappy. Make sure you build a church in your town.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits17=Church\r\ncontainer.sim.traits18=Attending Church\r\ncontainer.sim.traits19=Strong\r\ncontainer.sim.traits20=Strong folk can perform manual labour faster. Be it mining, cutting wood, building or digging sand.\r\ncontainer.sim.traits21=Workaholic\r\ncontainer.sim.traits22=Workaholic folk enjoy working, and will develop skills twice as fast as an ordinary folk. Unemployment makes these folk unhappy. Keep those employment rates up!\r\ncontainer.sim.ATTACKING=attacking\r\ncontainer.sim.ARRIVEDATFARM=arrived at farm\r\ncontainer.sim.ONPATROL=Patrolling\r\ncontainer.sim.SHEARING=shearing\r\ncontainer.sim.WAITINGFORWOOL=waiting for wool\r\ncontai